==Luxembourgish==

===Etymology===
Backformation from the comparative ''manner'', from {{inh|lb|gmh|minder}}, from {{inh|lb|goh|minniro||less; fewer}}, from {{inh|lb|gmw-pro|*minniʀō}}, from {{inh|lb|gem-pro|*minnizô}}, and/or reinterpretation (as a positive) of {{cog|goh|min||less}}, from {{cog|gem-pro|*minniz}}, adverbial form of the former.

Compare the same in {{cog|nl|min}}. The Luxembourgish vocalism is regular through ''-i-'' → ''-a-'' in closed syllables.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lb|/mɑn/}}
* {{rhymes|lb|ɑn|s=1}}
* {{homophones|lb|Mann}}

===Adjective===
{{lb-adj|mann|mann|comp=manner|comp-irreg-only=1|sup=mannsten}}

# [[little]], [[few]]

====Usage notes====
* The positive and comparative forms are indeclinable and cannot be preceded by articles or determiners. The superlative is declined in the normal way.

